<%# "All notes for you": the inbox in full, 50 a page, the same rows as the
    dashboard's card in the same order, narrowed by the filter (`@show`: all,
    unread or mentions, whose counts are `@counts`). "Mark all read" is there
    while something is unread (`notes_badge_count`, the sidebar's own number:
    asked once for both), and it is a secondary: the screen has no primary.
    The scope stays in a page's address and in the way back from a page
    beyond the last; All has no `show`.

    The screen is the lists' rail (`.admin-list-rail`): the grid holds the
    filter, the list and then the rail of open threads, in that order at every
    width, so the focus goes the same way. The rail is information, not a
    filter, which is why it follows the list; the grid docks it in the second
    column from 1200px of the screen's own width. It is read in
    `NoteInboxController#index` and never narrowed by the filter. %>
<% content_for :title, t(".page_title") %>
<% scope_params = @show == :all ? {} : { show: @show } %>
<div class="admin-list-rail">
  <div class="admin-list-rail__head">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink"><%= t(".title") %></h1>
    <% if notes_badge_count.positive? %>
      <%= button_to t(".mark_all_read"), admin_read_notes_path(**admin_url_options), class: Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.classes(:secondary, size: :small), form: { data: { turbo_frame: "_top" } } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="admin-list-rail__grid">
    <div class="mb-4 flex">
      <%= render Admin::Ui::TabLinksComponent.new(label: t(".filters.label"), link_data: { turbo_prefetch: false },
            tabs: Dashboard::NotesForYou::SHOWS.map { |show| { label: t(".filters.#{show}"), count: @counts.fetch(show), current: show == @show, href: admin_notes_path(**admin_url_options, **(show == :all ? {} : { show: show })) } }) %>
    </div>
    <% if @pagination.out_of_range? %>
      <div><%= render "admin/shared/out_of_range_page", url: admin_notes_path(**admin_url_options, **scope_params) %></div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="rounded-card bg-surface shadow-1">
        <% if @rows.empty? %>
          <% empty = @show == :all ? { title: t(".empty.all.title"), description: t(".empty.all.description") } : { title: t(".empty.#{@show}") } %>
          <%= render Admin::Ui::EmptyStateComponent.new(**empty) %>
        <% else %>
          <ul class="px-4">
            <% @rows.each do |row| %>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-line py-2.5 last:border-b-0"><%= render Admin::NotesScreen::InboxRowComponent.new(row: row) %></li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
          <%= render Admin::Ui::PaginationComponent.new(pagination: @pagination, url: ->(page) { admin_notes_path(**admin_url_options, **scope_params, page: page) }) %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Admin::NotesScreen::OpenThreadsComponent.new(threads: @threads) %>
  </div>
</div>
